# Machine-generated world snapshot (decision F6).
#
# Written by the dev-only POST /__claude-context endpoint in vite.config.js, so
# it regenerates on demand from the running app. Two reasons it is not tracked:
#
#   1. Churn — codex-entries.json alone is ~0.5 MB and every export produced a
#      fresh blob. It was the second-largest object in this repo's history.
#   2. It is the entire world (403 codex entries, 320 people, 52 houses), and
#      this repository is public.
#
# Consequence to be aware of: a fresh clone has no snapshot for a Claude session
# until you run an export. That is the intended trade.
#
# Note this does NOT remove the previously-committed copies from git history —
# they remain in past commits. See audit decision A2.
docs/claude-context/
